Description: resolved: add the root zone KSK-2024 (key tag 38696) to the built-in trust anchor
 Since 2026-10-11 the root zone DNSKEY RRset is signed only by KSK-2024.
 With DNSSEC=yes (or allow-downgrade against a DNSSEC-capable upstream)
 and no local trust anchor file, systemd-resolved trusts only KSK-2017
 (20326), so every lookup fails with "DNSSEC validation failed: missing-key".
Author: Lennart Poettering <lennart@poettering.net>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/systemd/systemd/commit/8113361e82eea2741290f7117034d356acb3ab4d
Bug: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/36260
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/systemd/+bug/2170538
Last-Update: 2026-10-12
